      "content": "Common criticisms against increased density often center on preserving neighborhood character and aesthetics. Residents frequently voice concerns about increased traffic congestion, strain on existing public infrastructure like schools and utilities, and the perceived loss of \"small-town feel.\" Another major issue is the potential for overcrowding and changes to neighborhood atmosphere, which can spark strong local opposition. Prepare to address these valid community concerns directly in your proposals.",
